{
  "_comment": [
    "GLOSSARY GRAPH — emitted once, on /encyclopedia/glossary/.",
    "",
    "WHAT FILLS THE PLACEHOLDERS — every term node is generated from an entry in",
    "data/glossary.json (180 entries). Nothing here is hand-written.",
    "",
    "  {{TERM_SLUG}}          glossary.json `slug` — the stable anchor and termCode.",
    "                         IMMUTABLE, exactly like an article slug: articles reference",
    "                         these @ids from their `about` arrays.",
    "  {{TERM_NAME}}          glossary.json `term`",
    "  {{TERM_DEFINITION}}    glossary.json `definition` — the one-sentence definition,",
    "                         verbatim, matching the visible text",
    "  {{TERM_ALTERNATE_N}}   glossary.json `alternateNames[]` — synonyms and acronyms",
    "  {{TERM_EXPLAINED_IN}}  glossary.json `explainedIn` — the article that explains the",
    "                         term in full, made absolute",
    "  {{TERM_SOURCE_URL}}    glossary.json `source.url` — the primary source for the",
    "                         definition (statute, CFR section, agency page)",
    "  {{TERM_WIKIDATA_URI}}  OPTIONAL. A Wikidata or Wikipedia URI for entity resolution.",
    "                         A human must verify each one against the actual entity.",
    "                         DELETE the sameAs property for any term without a verified",
    "                         match. A wrong sameAs asserts the term IS a different thing.",
    "",
    "  Two term nodes appear below as shape examples. Emit all 180.",
    "",
    "RULES",
    "  1. @id convention:  https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/#term-{{TERM_SLUG}}",
    "     Article graphs reference these exact @ids in `about`. Changing a term slug",
    "     breaks every article that points at it — treat slugs as immutable.",
    "  2. inDefinedTermSet points every member at #termset. Define the set once.",
    "  3. No Google rich result exists for DefinedTerm or DefinedTermSet. schema.org",
    "     lists them in the 'new' area (~10K-100K implementing domains). Emit for",
    "     semantic clarity and third-party consumers, expecting no Google benefit.",
    "  4. Every definition in the schema must appear verbatim in the visible glossary.",
    "  5. If glossary terms are ever split onto individual URLs, set each term's `url`",
    "     to its own page and keep the @id scheme unchanged so article refs still",
    "     resolve. 180 thin pages is a scaled-content risk; the single page is default."
  ],
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "DefinedTermSet",
      "@id": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/#termset",
      "name": "Grant Funding Glossary",
      "description": "A reference glossary of grant funding terms, each defined in one sentence with a primary-source citation and a link to the article that explains it in full.",
      "url": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/",
      "inLanguage": "en-US",
      "publisher": { "@id": "https://opengrants.io/#organization" },
      "hasDefinedTerm": [
        { "@id": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/#term-{{TERM_SLUG_1}}" },
        { "@id": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/#term-{{TERM_SLUG_2}}" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "DefinedTerm",
      "@id": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/#term-{{TERM_SLUG_1}}",
      "name": "{{TERM_NAME_1}}",
      "description": "{{TERM_DEFINITION_1}}",
      "termCode": "{{TERM_SLUG_1}}",
      "alternateName": ["{{TERM_ALTERNATE_1A}}", "{{TERM_ALTERNATE_1B}}"],
      "inDefinedTermSet": { "@id": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/#termset" },
      "url": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/#term-{{TERM_SLUG_1}}",
      "subjectOf": { "@id": "{{TERM_EXPLAINED_IN_1}}#article" },
      "citation": {
        "@type": "CreativeWork",
        "name": "{{TERM_SOURCE_NAME_1}}",
        "url": "{{TERM_SOURCE_URL_1}}"
      },
      "sameAs": "{{TERM_WIKIDATA_URI_1}}"
    },
    {
      "@type": "DefinedTerm",
      "@id": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/#term-{{TERM_SLUG_2}}",
      "name": "{{TERM_NAME_2}}",
      "description": "{{TERM_DEFINITION_2}}",
      "termCode": "{{TERM_SLUG_2}}",
      "alternateName": ["{{TERM_ALTERNATE_2A}}"],
      "inDefinedTermSet": { "@id": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/#termset" },
      "url": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/#term-{{TERM_SLUG_2}}",
      "subjectOf": { "@id": "{{TERM_EXPLAINED_IN_2}}#article" },
      "citation": {
        "@type": "CreativeWork",
        "name": "{{TERM_SOURCE_NAME_2}}",
        "url": "{{TERM_SOURCE_URL_2}}"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "@id": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/#webpage",
      "url": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/",
      "name": "Grant Funding Glossary",
      "description": "A reference glossary of grant funding terms, each defined in one sentence with a primary-source citation and a link to the article that explains it in full.",
      "isPartOf": { "@id": "https://opengrants.io/#website" },
      "breadcrumb": { "@id": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/#breadcrumb" },
      "mainEntity": { "@id": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/#termset" },
      "datePublished": "{{DATE_PUBLISHED}}",
      "dateModified": "{{DATE_MODIFIED}}",
      "inLanguage": "en-US"
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "@id": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/glossary/#breadcrumb",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 1,
          "name": "Home",
          "item": "https://opengrants.io/"
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 2,
          "name": "Encyclopedia",
          "item": "https://opengrants.io/encyclopedia/"
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 3,
          "name": "Grant Funding Glossary"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "@id": "https://opengrants.io/#organization"
    }
  ]
}
